  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner D-2 part 1">Scope: the additive path. A membership whose `sprk_enddate` has passed STOPS conferring access. Access must be re-granted explicitly; there is no grace period to invent.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner D-10 (2026-09-21)">🔴 Scope: the additive path, `sprk_startdate`. A membership whose `sprk_startdate` is in the FUTURE confers NOTHING yet — the owner's words: *"membership with future start date confers as of the access date."* Access begins ON the start date. Today the junction query bounds on `statecode` ALONE (`AccessibleRecordSetService.cs:478` states this outright) and NOTHING under `src/server/**` reads `sprk_startdate` — all 8 repo hits are client-side fixtures/UI — so a future-dated row with `statecode=0` confers access TODAY. That is the live gap this closes. **Mechanics mirror `sprk_enddate`, inverted in direction**: `(sprk_startdate eq null or sprk_startdate le {today:yyyy-MM-dd})`. The `eq null` branch is load-bearing because OData `le` EXCLUDES nulls and a membership with no start date is an ordinary current membership that MUST still confer; `le` not `lt` because the column is Date Only and access holds ON the start date, not from the day after. ⚠️ Do NOT mirror task 107's inversion of the null branch — that inversion is correct for a GRANT's `sprk_expiresdate` and applying it here would silently revoke every open-ended membership in the system. This is D-2 part 1's bound at the other end of the range.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner D-10 (2026-09-21)">Scope: the VETO subject, `sprk_startdate`. Unchanged and `statecode`-ONLY, exactly as D-2 part 2 ruled for `sprk_enddate`. A not-yet-started membership is STILL a wall subject: the org-keyed ethical wall over-matches by design, and date-bounding it in EITHER direction would be a fail-OPEN change to a veto. Both date bounds apply to the CONFERRING set only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner D-2 part 2">Scope: the veto subject. The FR-23 deny-veto subject stays on `statecode` ALONE and deliberately OVER-matches — an org-keyed ethical wall KEEPS binding a former member. Documented support: FR-23 (`spec.md:86`) and `AccessibleRecordSetService.cs:550-554` "Denial deliberately OVER-matches." Do NOT date-bound the veto; that would be a fail-OPEN change to a veto.</constraint>
    <constraint source="owner D-2 part 3">Scope: deployment. COUNT and LIST the date-ended-but-active rows, and the active grants under inactive organizations, BEFORE any behaviour ships. This change REMOVES live access.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task 043 / NFR-02">Scope: the read budget. ONE junction read per resolution, projecting everything both consumers need. A second query re-introduces the two-snapshot hazard task 043 removed and is not an acceptable implementation.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Scope: fail direction, per consumer. A fault must never GRANT (additive term contributes nothing) and must never silently UN-WALL (veto denies every candidate). Both must remain true simultaneously — that is the whole point of carrying an outcome rather than a list.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ExternalParticipationService.cs:1060-1069">Scope: the existing asymmetry. Preserve it. Close only the query-level-fault-for-the-veto hole; do not unify the two fail directions, and do not weaken the token-acquisition path that already denies.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §11">Scope: machinery. EXTEND `ActiveOrgMemberships` (`AccessibleRecordSetService.cs:457`) and the existing private junction query. No new service, no new outcome record, no second reader. Note that `ExternalOrganizationMembership` (`RevokeExternalAccessEndpoint.cs:667`) reads this junction in the INVERSE direction on a different client and is deliberately NOT merged (`:641-650`).</constraint>
    <constraint source="task 020">Scope: borrowed shapes. "Do not inherit the revoke's shape by default, because its fail direction is inverted relative to yours."</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Scope: this task's PR. Placement Justification; publish size vs a FRESH master worktree from a SHORT path with file counts compared on both sides; no new HIGH CVE; tests updated.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Scope: tests. KEEP path is `tests/integration/auth/**` (security-auth). The ArchTest guard correction belongs in `tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/`.</constraint>
  </constraints>

