  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Re-verify live metadata for `sprk_enddate` — its type and behaviour. It was UNVERIFIED at authoring because the Dataverse MCP server was DOWN (CONNECTION_CLOSED). If `sprk_enddate` is not Date Only, fire the escalation rather than choosing a comparison. 🟢 `sprk_startdate`'s existence is NO LONGER an open question: it EXISTS and is DATE ONLY (live-verified by task 117, `notes/task-117-reconcile-grant-and-membership-state.md:42`) — confirm the type still holds, but do not treat it as a discovery.</step>
    <step order="1">Measure the before-state and LIST it, now THREE categories: date-ended-but-still-active junction rows; **future-`sprk_startdate`-but-active rows (D-10 — these confer today and will stop)**; and active grants whose organization is inactive. This is D-2 part 3 plus D-10, and it gates any behaviour change. All three are access REMOVALS.</step>
    <step order="2">In the private junction query (`ExternalParticipationService.cs:1087`), project `sprk_enddate` **and `sprk_startdate`** alongside the org lookup and stop swallowing a non-success status into an empty list — report that the read could not be completed, while keeping the additive caller's empty-on-fault contribution.</step>
    <step order="3">Extend `ActiveOrgMemberships` to carry the two named sets — a date-bounded conferring set (bounded at BOTH ends per D-2 part 1 and D-10) and a statecode-only wall-subject set — and wire each consumer to the one it needs. Add the ISS-026 read guard so an inactive `sprk_organization` confers nothing, WITHOUT breaking the single-read invariant (if it cannot be expressed in one read, escalate rather than adding a second).</step>
    <step order="4">Correct the three retired-rule artifacts: the false comment (`:1081-1082`), the stale caveat (`:1083-1085`), and the guard test's justification plus its stale line reference (`ExternalAccessQueryIntegrityGuardTests.cs:54-57`).</step>
    <step order="5">Tests per the closed set; perturbations; build, full suite, ArchTests, publish size vs a fresh master; notes; TASK-INDEX rows for BOTH 109 and 110.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>`sprk_enddate`'s type/behaviour is UNVERIFIED. If it is DateTime/UserLocal rather than Date Only, a read-time date comparison is the wrong instrument and this belongs in a Dataverse-side deactivation instead (task 117) — owner decision D-2 names exactly this as the thing that would change the answer. STOP; do not pick a comparison.</trigger>
    <trigger>🟢 RETIRED 2026-09-21 — ANSWERED, do not fire. This trigger read: "If `sprk_startdate` exists, a not-yet-STARTED membership is a second fail direction this task never scoped. STOP rather than widening scope silently." `sprk_startdate` DOES exist (DATE ONLY, live-verified by task 117), and the owner answered it as **decision D-10**: *"membership with future start date confers as of the access date."* It is now IN SCOPE as a constraint below, not an escalation. Escalate only if live metadata contradicts the DATE ONLY finding.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the Step 1 count shows more than a handful of rows losing access, that is an access-removal event needing owner sign-off before anything ships — not an implementation detail. STOP and report the counts and the list.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the ISS-026 organization-statecode guard cannot be satisfied within ONE read (e.g. it needs an expand Dataverse will not serve), that is a decision about task 043's single-snapshot invariant, not a free choice. STOP and present the options with a recommendation.</trigger>
  </escalation>

