  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">ADDITIVE, positive: a membership with a null `sprk_enddate`, or one whose `sprk_enddate` is today or later, still confers inherited access — access holds THROUGH the end date, mirroring `ExpiryPredicate`'s boundary.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ADDITIVE, negative: a membership whose `sprk_enddate` has passed confers NOTHING, even though its `statecode` is still active.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">🔴 ADDITIVE, negative (D-10): a membership whose `sprk_startdate` is in the FUTURE confers NOTHING, even though its `statecode` is active. This is the live access gap at HEAD.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ADDITIVE, positive (D-10): a membership whose `sprk_startdate` is TODAY confers access — the boundary is inclusive, matching `ExpiryPredicate`'s `ge`/`le` convention for Date Only columns; and a membership with a NULL `sprk_startdate` still confers, because no start bound means an ordinary current membership. A test must pin the null case explicitly — inverting it would silently revoke every open-ended membership.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">VETO, unchanged (D-10): an org-keyed deny row still matches a subject whose membership has NOT YET STARTED — the wall stays `statecode`-only at BOTH ends of the range, and a test asserts this over-match explicitly so a later "consistency" fix cannot date-bound the veto.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Perturbation (D-10): removing the start-date bound makes the future-dated test go green again; inverting its null branch reddens the null-start-date test. Both reverted before completion.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">VETO, unchanged: an org-keyed deny row still matches a subject whose membership has ENDED by date — the wall over-matches by design, and a test asserts the over-match explicitly so a later "consistency" fix cannot silently date-bound it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">🔴 VETO on a query fault: an HTTP 500/403/timeout on the junction query now denies every queried candidate instead of reading as "belongs to no organization". This is the ISS-019 fix and the single most important assertion in this task.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ADDITIVE on the same fault: the additive term contributes NOTHING — the fault must not grant. Both fail directions hold simultaneously, from one read.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The pre-existing token/API-url-acquisition fail-closed path still denies (it must not be weakened by the new fault reporting).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ISS-026 read guard: an active grant and an active membership whose parent `sprk_organization` is INACTIVE confer nothing; an active organization is unaffected; a contact-keyed grant with no organization lookup is unaffected.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Exactly ONE junction read per resolution — asserted, not assumed (count the reads in a test). Task 043's single-snapshot invariant and the NFR-02 budget hold.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A row whose `statecode` is NULL is treated as ACTIVE, matching `ExternalGrantLifecycle.IsActive` (`:121`) semantics.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`ActiveOrgMemberships` was EXTENDED — no second outcome record and no second junction reader was introduced anywhere (verified by grep).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The false comment at `:1081-1082` and the stale caveat at `:1083-1085` are corrected, and the guard test's justification at `ExternalAccessQueryIntegrityGuardTests.cs:54-57` no longer says a membership row has no expiry; its stale `:1068` reference points at the real junction query.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The Step 1 before-state (counts plus the row list, both categories) is recorded in the task notes before any behaviour change is merged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Perturbation: reverting the fault reporting makes the veto-on-fault test go green again; removing the date bound makes the ended-membership test go green again; date-bounding the VETO subject reddens the over-match test. All three reverted before completion.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build green; full suite green; ArchTests green; publish size reported against a fresh master with equal file counts on both sides and ≤60 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes. Do not add near-identical happy-path variants.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Authored 2026-09-19 (session 17) via /task-create, consolidating ISS-019 + ISS-020 + ISS-026's read half.

⚠️ THIS TASK SUBSUMES TASK 110. They are ONE change (plan §3, owner brief D-2): one read, projecting what both consumers need, returning an outcome plus two named sets. Task 110's POML records that it is executed here. Completing this task closes **#998** and **#999**, and the READ half of **#1006** — whose WRITE half is task 117.

SCOPING JUDGMENT, recorded 2026-09-19: ISS-026's READ guard lives here rather than in task 117 because it touches the same query this task is already rewriting as a single snapshot. Putting it in the scheduled job would split one query's correctness across two tasks and re-introduce the hazard task 043 removed. 117 owns only the WRITE (deactivating the rows so `statecode` becomes the truth). Once 117 has run, this read-time guard becomes belt-and-braces rather than load-bearing — keep it anyway; it is the fail-closed half.

⚠️ THIS PROJECT HAS 19 PRIOR INSTANCES OF PREMISE ROT (`notes/task-accuracy-audit-2026-09-18.md:9`). Every load-bearing claim above was checked against source on 2026-09-19 with file and line recorded so you can re-check cheaply — verify anyway, because the code has won every time. The two deliberately UNVERIFIED claims are named in the escalation triggers, and they are unverified because the Dataverse MCP server was down, not because nobody looked. One claim in the earlier record was outright FALSE and is corrected in the background above: "exposure is nil" covered only the standing-gated org-EXPANSION term, not the org-GRANT term.

Register: `notes/defer-issues.md` § ISS-019, § ISS-020, § ISS-026. Related: tasks 020, 042, 043, 107, 117.</notes>

